        "original_id": "29e5a976-44d6-5b1d-a6c9-b0d122998db6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Inula, Fouquieria, Dittrichia, Fouquieria formosa\n- Taxonomy: Asteraceae, Fouquieriaceae, genera, species\n- Places: Europe, Asia, Africa, central and southern Mexico\n\nFacts:\n- Inula is a large genus of about 90 species of flowering plants in the family Asteraceae that is native to Europe, Asia, and Africa.\n- Fouquieria is a genus of 11 species of desert plants and is the sole genus in the family Fouquieriaceae.\n- Dittrichia species were formerly included in the genus Inula.\n- Fouquieria formosa is a species of Fouquieria in the ocotillo family that is native to central and southern Mexico, including Chiapas, Oaxaca, Guerrero, Puebla, Morelos, Michoacán, México State, Distrito Federal, and Jalisco.",
